Hello!
So, in my game the party is comprised of a single hero with 6 accessories able to be equipped. For balance reasons, the player is only able to earn 3 of any accessory in the game.
For the following example, for ease, I'll simply call the accessory "Ribbon."
My ribbon has the note tag  <Max Item: 3>
The notetag works perfectly in shops, only allowing me to buy 3 Ribbons.
HOWEVER, if I equip all 3 Ribbons, and go back into the store, I can buy another 3 Ribbons.
I understand this is likely due to the plugin not including equipment when considering max items.
I found another thread with a similar issue, and the proposed code was as follows:
Game_Party.prototype.numItems = function(item)
{
var container = this.itemContainer(item);
let numHeld = container ? container[item.id] || 0 : 0;
if (container == this._weapons)
$gameActors._data.forEach(actor =>
{
if (actor)
actor.weapons().forEach(weapon => {if (weapon.id == item.id || weapon.baseItemId && weapon.baseItemId == item.id) numHeld++;});
});
else if (container == this._armors)
$gameActors._data.forEach(actor =>
{
if (actor)
actor.armors().forEach(armor=> {if (armor.id == item.id || armor.baseItemId && armor.baseItemId == item.id) numHeld++;});
});
return numHeld;
};
Whilst this code works in the shop preventing me from owning more than 3, it presents a new unique issue - it resulted in infinite ribbons. If I equipped one, my number of ribbons would actually go up, which makes sense looking at the code. If I had 3 ribbons equipped, and 3 in my inventory, my total ribbons in my inventory would appear as 6, essentially giving me 9 ribbons.
My question is essentially, how can I make the shop follow the max item cap including the equipment my actor has equipped? Or is there a way to modify this code to ONLY be considered when inside the shop?
Any suggestions at all would be immensely appreciated, thank you!

