When you're referencing something you got from another post, you should always link to that post - that way people know what you're talking about and you won't get duplicate effort/results.
As a side note, when you post code, use the CODE tags - the </> on the edit bar - so that it's legible and the forum doesn't eat your brackets.
Note that's explicitly how the OP of that thread
wanted
it to work - they wanted the number you see anyplace to reflect the total number of that item that you own, whether it's in your inventory, equipped, etc.
If you want to quickly modify that snippet so that it only applies in the shop scene, then you'd do this:
Code:
Game_Party.prototype.numItems = function(item)
{
    var container = this.itemContainer(item);
    let numHeld = container ? container[item.id] || 0 : 0;
    if (container == this._weapons && SceneManager._scene typeof Scene_Shop)
        $gameActors._data.forEach(actor =>
        {
             if (actor)
                actor.weapons().forEach(weapon => {if (weapon.id == item.id || weapon.baseItemId && weapon.baseItemId == item.id) numHeld++;});
        });
    else if (container == this._armors && SceneManager._scene typeof Scene_Shop)
        $gameActors._data.forEach(actor =>
        {
             if (actor)
                actor.armors().forEach(armor=> {if (armor.id == item.id || armor.baseItemId && armor.baseItemId == item.id) numHeld++;});
        });
    return numHeld;
};
I don't know if this shop scene also displays the number carried anyplace that this would mess with - if that's the case, then what
@Robro33
suggested would be a more elegant fix to have it interface directly with the buying method.
But this should cause the shop to count weapons and armor equipped where looking at held items in the main menu will not.
